Got it. You do **not** want to stream application/business data from YugabyteDB tables using CDC.

You want:

> **YugabyteDB server logs → Kafka → Druid → Grafana/Superset**

For example:

* database errors
* slow queries
* connection logs
* transaction failures
* audit events
* node health events
* latency metrics
* operational events

This is a **log analytics / observability POC**, not a data analytics CDC pipeline.

The architecture changes slightly:

```text
              YugabyteDB Cluster
              (3 Nodes)
              
        yb-node1   yb-node2   yb-node3
            |          |          |
            |          |          |
        Server Logs  Server Logs  Server Logs
            |          |          |
            +----------+----------+
                       |
                       v
              Log Collector
          (Fluent Bit / Filebeat)
                       |
                       v
                  Apache Kafka
                       |
              Topic: yugabyte-logs
                       |
                       v
              Druid Kafka Ingestion
                       |
                       v
             Druid Datasource
              yb_server_logs
                       |
                       v
          Grafana / Apache Superset
```

